<http://data.silknow.org/object/86fb52f5-d2ab-394c-af1c-722c06987bd8>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Tapestry woven in silk and wool. The tapestry is framed with borders of military trophies with a larger trophy of flags and lances at the centre top surmounted by trumpets crossed through a laurel wreath. The trophy in the centre of the lower border has bundles of staves, axes and weapons.\n\nThe central scene shows a mounted officer in the foreground supervising the collection of wood, while other soldiers chop down trees, cut branches and bind them into bundles. Behind them, three men are riding off with bundles through groups of men similarly occupied to a distant camp. A cuirass and jacket lie discarded in the left corner."@en , "Tapestry 'Cutting Fascine' woven in silk and wool, from the series 'The Art of War', designed by Philipp De Hondt, woven by Judocus de Vos, Brussels, 1718-1719"@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/e355dd13-5284-3e59-9ea8-38f45547cb5a> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/256362f5-346d-3265-8bea-6ebd22e2b60c> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Tapestry woven in silk and wool. The tapestry is framed with borders of military trophies with a larger trophy of flags and lances at the centre top surmounted by trumpets crossed through a laurel wreath. The trophy in the centre of the lower border has bundles of staves, axes and weapons.\n\nThe central scene shows a mounted officer in the foreground supervising the collection of wood, while other soldiers chop down trees, cut branches and bind them into bundles. Behind them, three men are riding off with bundles through groups of men similarly occupied to a distant camp. A cuirass and jacket lie discarded in the left corner."@en , "Tapestry 'Cutting Fascine' woven in silk and wool, from the series 'The Art of War', designed by Philipp De Hondt, woven by Judocus de Vos, Brussels, 1718-1719"@en ;
